From 03e986dad31411c905a0a7c577b326bcac307362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 05:38:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): machine sessions never own a card, whatever
 their id shape [daveey]

resolve_chats took any unreleased link unless is_headless_session() (local-<sha256> only) rejected it,
so older Kanban worker transcripts (timestamp ids), cron runs (cron_<job>_<ts>) and one-shots counted as
the nearest human chat. #594's live proof (hub example-card) resolved to MacBook worker transcript
example-session instead of creator_chats_unresolved.

- kanban_db_notify.is_machine_session(gateway, session): headless id, cron_ id, or a session of THIS
  gateway whose state.db source is kanban/cron/oneshot/subagent (batch: machine_sessions). Missing,
  unknown or foreign sessions stay human.
- resolve_chats (incl. _chat_links' hub-sub branch) and _inherit_notify_subs skip them and keep walking.
- kanban_chat_links.reconcile no longer wants links to local machine sessions, so it releases them
  through its captured writes (they sync), including owner-written links on other gateways' open cards;
  each pass that releases any writes ~/.hermes/kanban/repairs/machine-links-<board>-<ts>-<n>.json.
- hermes kanban sync machine-links [--release]: dry run / release now.
